sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
After parsing, check the broad shape before the rest of the program depends on it.

```js
const rawBooks = '[{"title":"North Star"},{"title":"Deep Blue"}]';
const books = JSON.parse(rawBooks);

if (Array.isArray(books)) {
  console.log(`Loaded ${books.length} books`);
} else {
  console.log("Expected a book list");
}
```

Step by step:

1. Parse the JSON text.
2. `Array.isArray(books)` checks the broad collection shape.
3. Only the array path uses `.length` as a collection count.
4. The fallback makes a bad assumption visible.

This is a beginner validation habit, not full schema validation.

